# Backend Standards

Technology

Go Fiber v3

PostgreSQL

Ent ORM

Redis

JWT

RBAC

Swagger

Atlas Migration

Koanf

Zerolog

---

# Architecture

Always follow:

Controller

↓

Service

↓

Repository

↓

Database

Never bypass layers.

---

# Controller

Controllers should:

Validate input.

Call service.

Return response.

Nothing else.

Never place business logic here.

---

# Service

Service contains:

Business Rules

Validation

Authorization

Transactions

Calculations

---

# Repository

Responsible only for:

Database access.

No business logic.

---

# DTO

Never expose database entities directly.

Always use DTOs.

---

# Validation

Validate every request.

Never trust user input.

---

# Error Handling

Return consistent API responses.

Never expose internal errors.

Log internal errors.

Return friendly messages.

---

# Authentication

JWT Access Token

Refresh Token Rotation

Password Hashing using bcrypt.

---

# Authorization

RBAC.

Never check roles inside controllers.

Use middleware.

---

# Logging

Log:

Errors

Warnings

Security events

Authentication events

Never log:

Passwords

Tokens

Secrets

---

# Transactions

Use transactions whenever:

Multiple tables are modified.

---

# API Design

RESTful.

Versioned.

/api/v1

Future ready for /api/v2

---

# Database

Use Ent.

Never execute raw SQL unless necessary.

---

# Performance

Prevent N+1 queries.

Use indexes.

Paginate large datasets.

---

# Security

Sanitize inputs.

Validate uploads.

Rate limit authentication endpoints.

Protect against SQL injection.

Protect against XSS.

Protect against CSRF where applicable.

---

# Quality Checklist

✓ Layer respected

✓ Validation

✓ Authorization

✓ Logging

✓ Transactions

✓ DTO

✓ Tests

✓ Documentation